 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
 *   **Precision**: For large scenes, subtracting large world coordinates from the camera origin may cause floating-point precision loss [G].
+*   **Degenerate Input**: If $M_{c2w}$ contains non-uniform scaling or shearing, $R$ will not be orthogonal and $R^T \neq R^{-1}$, requiring a proper inverse or SVD decomposition instead of a simple transpose [G].
 
